g\n\n### Error: "STDMAE not found"\n- Check if model is registered in task_config.json\n- Ensure STDMAE.json exists in config/model/traffic_state_pred/\n- Verify STDMAE.py exists in libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/\n\n### Error: "CUDA out of memory"\n- Reduce batch_size: `--batch_size 32`\n- Reduce long_history_window in config: `"long_history_window": 576`\n\n### Poor convergence\n- Check learning rate: reduce to 0.0005\n- Verify data normalization: scaler should be "standard"\n- Increase patience for early stopping: `--patience 20`\n\n### NaN losses\n- Enable gradient clipping in config: `"max_grad_norm": 1.0`\n- Check data for missing values\n- Reduce learning rate to 0.0005\n\n## Citation\n\n```bibtex\n@article{liang2023stdmae,\n  title={STD-MAE: Spatio-Temporal-Decoupled Masked Pre-training for Traffic Forecasting},\n  author={Liang, Yixiao and others},\n  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2312.00516},\n  year={2023}\n}\n```\n\n## Version Info\n\n- **Model**: STD-MAE (Spatio-Temporal Dual Masked Autoencoder)\n- **LibCity Integration**: January 2026\n- **Paper**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00516\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/STD-MAE\n\n'}
