vice from config\n     * Initialize model architecture\n   - Implement `predict(batch)`:\n     * Extract batch['X'] with shape [B, T, N, C]\n     * Handle long_history if needed (for STDMAE)\n     * Return predictions [B, T, N, C]\n   - Implement `calculate_loss(batch)`:\n     * For TMAE/SMAE: compute masked reconstruction loss\n     * For STDMAE: compute forecasting loss (MAE)\n     * Use self._scaler for denormalization if needed\n\n3. **Handle Model-Specific Requirements:**\n   - **TMAE/SMAE:** Set spatial=False/True, mask_ratio=0.75 for pre-training\n   - **STDMAE:** Load pre-trained TMAE/SMAE checkpoints, freeze encoder parameters\n   - **Long History:** Support long_history_data input (864 timesteps vs 12 for history)\n   - **GraphWaveNet:** Adapt backend with adaptive adjacency matrix\n\n4. **Data Format Adaptations:**\n   - LibCity batch['X']: [B, T, N, C] → model expects [B, L, N, C]\n   - LibCity batch['y']: [B, T, N, C] → targets\n   - Handle adjacency matrix loading from data_feature\n   - Support feature selection (FORWARD_FEATURES=[0,1])\n\n5. **Critical Implementation Details:**\n   - Patch embedding with patch_size=12\n   - Mask generator for random masking\n   - Positional encoding (2D for spatial models)\n   - Transformer encoder/decoder with configurable depth\n   - GraphWaveNet with dilated convolutions and GCN\n\n6. **Register Models:**\n   - Update `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/__init__.py` to include TMAE, SMAE, STDMAE\n   - Add to appropriate model registry\n\n**Testing Checklist:**\n- [ ] Models can be imported without errors\n- [ ] TMAE/SMAE can forward pass with [B, L, N, C] input\n- [ ] STDMAE can load pre-trained checkpoints\n- [ ] calculate_loss returns valid scalar\n- [ ] predict returns correct shape\n\n**Reference Existing Models:** Check STID, PatchTST, or BigST in LibCity for patterns.\n\n**Note:** Focus on STDMAE first (the main fine-tuning model), then TMAE/SMAE can be simplified versions for pre-training if needed.", 'subagent